// ====================================================================================================
// PROVIDER MANIFEST
// ====================================================================================================
//
// What this does:
//   This is the single source of truth for which providers are available, what media types they
//   support, what capabilities they expose (streaming / downloading / subtitles), which external ID
//   systems they can use for lookup, and the order in which they are tried. The provider registry at
//   startup reads this file and builds the provider dispatch table from it. A provider module that
//   exists on disk but is not registered here is NEVER loaded or called.
//
// Fields (one entry per provider):
//   name           Provider identifier. Must match the exported function name in the module:
//                  <name>Streams (streaming) or <name>Downloads (downloading).
//   module         Path to the provider module relative to this manifest (e.g. "./castle.ts").
//   enabled        true to make the provider available; false to register it without using it.
//                  Disabled providers are ignored during priority conflict detection.
//   type           Media types this provider serves: "movies", "series", "anime".
//   capabilities   Operations this provider can perform: "streaming" and/or "downloading".
//                  (A future "subtitle" capability would enable standalone subtitle fetching.)
//   supportedIds   ID systems this provider can actually use for lookup or matching:
//                  "tmdb", "imdb", "anilist", "mal", "moviebox". Providers that rely purely on
//                  title/fuzzy search get an empty array [].
//                  Providers supporting multiple ID systems (e.g. both "anilist" and "mal")
//                  can list them all — the health checker and metadata layer will pass
//                  all available IDs and the provider chooses which to use.
//                  NOTE: this field is descriptive configuration for registration and selection.
//                  It does NOT perform ID translation — the metadata layer still owns spun_id and
//                  external-ID associations.
//   priority_stream      (optional) Fallback priority for streaming. Lower number = tried first.
//   priority_download    (optional) Fallback priority for downloading. Lower number = tried first.
//
// Valid media types: "movies", "series", "anime"
//
// Valid capabilities: "streaming", "downloading"
//
// Valid ID systems: "tmdb", "imdb", "anilist", "mal", "moviebox"
//
// How priorities work:
//   For a given media type + capability combination (e.g. movies/streaming), providers are sorted
//   by their priority_* value ascending. The first provider returning at least one result wins;
//   empty results cause fallback to the next provider.
//
// Priority conflicts:
//   Two enabled providers may NOT share the same priority for the same media type + capability.
//   On startup the registry detects this, logs a clear warning naming the providers, the media
//   type, the capability and the colliding priority, and SKIPS ALL providers involved in that
//   specific conflict for that operation only. It does not disable the provider for other
//   capabilities/media types. Conflicts are never silently resolved by alphabetical order or
//   manifest position. A provider missing a required priority for a declared capability is
//   skipped for that operation with a warning and does not crash the layer.
//
// Registering a new provider:
//   1. Implement the provider as a module at the path given by "module" in this manifest.
//      - Streaming providers must export "get<Name>Streams" (e.g. getCastleStreams).
//      - Downloading providers must export "get<Name>Downloads" (e.g. getMovieboxDownloads).
//      The registry dynamically imports the module and resolves these exports by name.
//   2. Add one entry to this manifest with the correct name/module/capabilities/types/priorities.
//   3. No other orchestration code needs to change.
//
// ====================================================================================================

{
  "providers": [
    {
      "name": "anikoto",
      "module": "./anikoto.ts",
      "enabled": true,
      "type": ["anime"],
      "capabilities": ["streaming"],
